  "result": "**Root cause:** `buildChargePayload` (`src/payments/gateway/payload.js`) lower-cases the currency (`jpy`) for the gateway and then passes that lower-case code to `toMinor`. The currency registry only has upper-case keys, so `jpy` and `krw` weren't found. The lookup fell back to the default exponent of 2, which turned ¥1,500 into 150,000. USD and EUR looked fine because their exponent is 2 anyway.\n\n**Fix:** In `src/lib/currency/registry.js`, `exponent`, `isSupported` and `symbol` now trim and upper-case the code before looking it up. This fixes the charge payload, and it also protects other callers that might pass a lower-case code, such as refunds, payouts, coupons and dunning fees.\n\n**Regression tests:** I added two tests to `test/charge.test.js`. A JPY invoice of 1500 must produce a charge amount of 1500, and a KRW invoice of 20000 must produce 20000.\n\n`npm test` passes: 8 of 8 tests. I didn't run the new tests against the old code to confirm they fail there.",
